<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    strings_jemma.xml — Japanese (ja).
    Translation of the EN default strings_jemma.xml (in values/).

    Japanese conventions used here :
      • Polite plain (です・ます) form throughout — appropriate for an emergency
        product where the tone must be reassuring but not too casual
      • Medical / clinical terms use the standard Japanese FHIR-JP conventions
        when they exist (患者リソース, アレルギー, etc.); ATC/SNOMED kept in latin
      • Shikoku / pilgrim cultural cues preserved (the SOS scenario takes
        place during a Shikoku earthquake with Haru as the elderly Japanese
        victim — see the storytelling in the writeup)
-->
